Alignment file: this file shows one nucleotide sequence of Cytochrome C aligned with 3 other sequences. 
Each stretch is 60 nucleotides long, aligned with nucleotides of other species. 
The gaps (-) show that insertions or deletions may have occured as part of evolutionary changes in the sequence.
The asterisk (*) means that that specific nucleotide has been conserved (remains the same) throughout all the sequences being aligned.
Guide tree: it is an order in which the sequences are aligned on the basis of similarity. Most similar sequences are aligned first and so on.
Phylogenetic tree: it is intended to show the true evolutionary history of the sequences after the sequences are aligned, 
to show which species are more closely related than others.
